            <ArticleTitle>[The effect of clofelin on the pain syndrome in mandibular trauma].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>20-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Oral clopheline (0.000075) noticeably alleviates the pain syndrome and circulatory hyperdynamic state of patients with mandibular fracture. The agent is superior to the conventional combination of 50% analgin (2 ml) and 1% dimedrolum (1 ml) in its efficiency and duration of action.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
